div.p:
—U.S. ability to exert leverage is limited since U.S. farm and free trade
                    interests will oppose any attempt to limit sales in reaction to unwanted Soviet
                    behavior, and any government controls are likely to be short-lived;

note.p:
SNIE 11–6–76, “Implications of the 1975 Soviet Harvest,” dated February 10;
                    attached but not printed. A copy is in Central Intelligence Agency, Electronic
                    Reading Room.
